damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Sailing in the Salt Flat is a hazardous affair to begin with, but some sailors seek even greater thrills, such as hanging from a flying fin, or firing themselves from saltheap cannons. Those who survive tend to go to even more extreme lengths to satisfy their thirst for danger.","abilities":["Movement Speed increases briefly when crossing a Rope Bridge or launched by a <Saltheap Cannon>"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.9,"stats":{"hp":6500,"atk":420,"def":60,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2}},"unlucky_flyfin":{"slug":"unlucky_flyfin","name":"Unlucky Flyfin","icon":"/enemies-icons/Unlucky Flyfin.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":null,"damageType":["No Damage"],"flavourText":"A male fin that leaps out of the salt layer during breeding season, gliding briefly in mid-air and releasing unpleasant pheromones. Having one fall onto the deck is seen as an omen of bad luck.","abilities":["Low-Altitude Hovering; after losing Low-Altitude Hovering, becomes stunned for some time before taking off again","Movement Speed briefly increases after taking damage for the first time. Sometimes carries <Risk-surviving Sailor>"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.6,"stats":{"hp":12000,"atk":100,"def":0,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":1}},"saltfin_breaker":{"slug":"saltfin_breaker","name":"Saltfin Breaker","icon":"/enemies-icons/Saltfin Breaker.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Despite its size and weight, this saltfin is surprisingly lithe when swimming through the salts. Normally gentle in nature, it can shatter even hardened ancient salt layers with its powerful slamming attacks when provoked.","abilities":["Attacks deal Physical splash damage to all nearby allied units","Immune to the effects of Salt Flat and gains increased Movement Speed while in Salt Flat"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":100000,"atk":2000,"def":0,"res":0,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":6}},"bridge_builder":{"slug":"bridge_builder","name":"Bridge Builder","icon":"/enemies-icons/Bridge Builder.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Portable and quick to build, rope bridges are a convenient way to connect two salt ships. Bridge builders are responsible for constructing them, but they still need others to help hold them in place and prevent them from falling apart.","abilities":["Invisible","Builds rope bridges that allow units to cross"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.65,"stats":{"hp":6000,"atk":600,"def":150,"res":30,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2}},"terrible_chef":{"slug":"terrible_chef","name":"Terrible Chef","icon":"/enemies-icons/Terrible Chef.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"More butcher than cook, the fleet's chefs are more adept at dismembering carcasses than making the aftermath fit for human consumption. No sailor who has seen one dismember a saltfin has the guts to complain about their cooking.","abilities":["More likely to be attacked","Nearby enemies and <Saltheap Cannons> take far less Physical/Arts damage from sources in the direction of the shield"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.5,"stats":{"hp":20000,"atk":1200,"def":1800,"res":40,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5}}},"dropIcons":{"4002":"/item-icons/originite_prime.png","act39side_token_garum_rep_1":"/item-icons/saltfin_garum_act39side_token_garum_rep_1.png"},"previewFile":"